      "summary": "ASML Stocks Surge 3.5% as Samsung Pulls High-NA Into DRAM TradingView",
      "body": "ASML Stocks Surge 3.5% as Samsung Pulls High-NA Into DRAM\nASML Holding ASML, the semiconductor-lithography equipment leader, deepened its Samsung (SSNLF) partnership around High-NA EUV and larger photomasks, while U.S. shares climbed approximately 3.5% to $1,870.48 at about 12:20 a.m. ET Friday. The September 8 agreement gives investors another reason to watch memory-chip manufacturing as a market for ASML's most advanced machines. The opportunity is bigger. The revenue still needs to follow.\nSamsung plans to bring High-NA EUV into high-volume DRAM production by 2028 and help develop a 12-inch photomask platform. ASML expects the larger format to lift manufacturing productivity, lower chipmaking costs and eliminate stitching constraints. For investors, the attraction is straightforward: adoption in memory could broaden demand for technology already aimed at leading-edge logic chips.\nThe valuation leaves little room for delays: the picture shows shares trading 47.7% above the roughly $1",
